---
layout: base.njk
---
  <header class="hero">
    <nav class="topnav wrap-wide" aria-label="Site">
{%- if collections.posts and collections.posts.length %}
      <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
{%- endif %}
      <a href="#download">Download</a>
      <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <h1 class="logo">
        <img src="/img/logo-1000.webp" srcset="/img/logo-600.webp 600w, /img/logo-1000.webp 1000w"
             sizes="(max-width: 640px) 86vw, 34rem" width="1000" height="619" alt="{{ site.title }}">
      </h1>
      <p class="tagline">A bubble shooter in three dimensions. The cluster hangs from a sheet of glass and sways when you hit it, and whatever you cut loose falls.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button" href="{{ site.download }}">Download for Windows</a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="#download">Raspberry Pi 5, and how to run it</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note">Free · Windows 10 and 11, 64-bit · about 400&nbsp;MB · nothing to install. Windows warns you the first time you run it: <a href="#download">why, and what to click</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-shot wrap-wide">
      <img src="/img/shots/meander-1600.jpg" srcset="/img/shots/meander-800.jpg 800w, /img/shots/meander-1600.jpg 1600w"
           sizes="(max-width: 1184px) 100vw, 74rem" width="1600" height="900"
           alt="A cluster of coloured balls hangs under glass over a stone island; behind it a volcano pours lava, and the cannon points up at the cluster.">
      <figcaption>Meander, in The Eruption. Every picture on this page is the game itself, as you play it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="section" id="play" aria-labelledby="play-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="play-title">How it plays</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Fire up into it</h3>
            <p>A cluster of coloured balls hangs above a stone island. You stand under it with a cannon: turn it, raise the barrel, fire. A shot sticks where it lands.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>Match, and bring it down</h3>
            <p>Three or more of a colour touching, and the group falls, with everything that was hanging from it. The shot to look for is rarely the biggest clump. It is the one ball holding a lot of others up.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>It really hangs</h3>
            <p>Every ball is held to its neighbours and the top row to the glass, in a real physics simulation. Hit the cluster and it sways; cut what holds a branch and the branch drops.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3>The glass comes down</h3>
            <p>Every few shots the glass steps down and the cluster with it. If the cluster reaches the red line, the level is lost, so your clock is your own shots.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section numbers" aria-label="The campaign in numbers">
      <div class="wrap numbers-row">
        <p><strong>{{ site.levels }}</strong> levels</p>
        <p><strong>{{ site.chapters }}</strong> chapters</p>
        <p><strong>{{ site.scenes }}</strong> scenes</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section live" id="cannon" aria-labelledby="cannon-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="cannon-title">The cannon, live</h2>
        <p class="lead">This is the game's own cannon, drawn in your browser from the very meshes the game builds. It drives round on omni wheels, rolling forward or crabbing sideways on their rollers, and fires now and then.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="wrap-wide">
        <div class="cannon-stage">
          <canvas class="cannon-canvas" width="1600" height="900" role="img" aria-label="The game's cannon drives round a circle on omni wheels and fires a coloured ball from its barrel."></canvas>
          <button class="cannon-pause" type="button" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Pause</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <script type="module" src="/js/cannon.js"></script>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="gallery" aria-labelledby="gallery-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="gallery-title">Every chapter somewhere else</h2>
        <p class="lead">From a meadow to a volcano, deep space and a circus tent, each chapter has a scene of its own and music of its own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery wrap">
{%- for shot in gallery %}
        <figure>
          <a href="/img/shots/{{ shot.file }}-1600.jpg">
            <img src="/img/shots/{{ shot.file }}-800.jpg" srcset="/img/shots/{{ shot.file }}-800.jpg 800w, /img/shots/{{ shot.file }}-1600.jpg 1600w"
                 sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1040px) 50vw, 32rem" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy"
                 alt="{{ shot.level }}, a level of {{ shot.chapter }}: {{ shot.caption | lower }}.">
          </a>
          <figcaption><strong>{{ shot.level }}</strong>, {{ shot.chapter }}. {{ shot.caption }}.</figcaption>
        </figure>
{%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="wrap">
{%- if site.video %}
        <p class="video"><a class="button button-quiet" href="{{ site.video }}">Watch it in motion</a></p>
{%- else %}
        <p class="later">A video of it in motion is on its way.</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- if collections.posts and collections.posts.length %}
        <p class="later">How it is made (the lattice, the Pi renderer, the music) is told <a href="/blog/">on the blog</a>.</p>
{%- endif %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="features-title">What else is in it</h2>
        <ul class="features">
          <li><strong>Odd balls and power-ups.</strong> Bombs, glass, stone, buckshot and more turn up as the campaign goes on, each shown to you the first time you meet it. From the third chapter you carry power-ups too: a swap, a brake for the ceiling, a cut.</li>
          <li><strong>Stars, scores and leaderboards.</strong> Every level has a score and up to four stars, and online leaderboards for this month and all time. They are off until you choose a nickname and switch them on; nothing is sent before that.</li>
          <li><strong>Colours you can tell apart by shape.</strong> Every colour wears a pattern of its own, stripes, spots, checks or a printed symbol, so two colours that look alike still differ.</li>
          <li><strong>Mouse and keyboard, or a controller.</strong> On an Xbox controller you feel the game in your hands, the triggers' own motors included.</li>
          <li><strong>Made in code.</strong> The balls, the cannon, the island, the skies, the scenery and the sound effects are not bought or modelled: the game makes them itself.</li>
          <li><strong>A Raspberry Pi 5 version</strong>, from the same release and on the same leaderboards.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
{%- if collections.posts and collections.posts.length %}

    <section class="section" id="workshop" aria-labelledby="workshop-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="workshop-title">From the workshop</h2>
        <p class="lead">What we ran into while making it, and what we did about it.</p>
        <ul class="posts">
{%- for post in collections.posts | reverse %}
{%- if loop.index <= 3 %}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a> <time datetime="{{ post.date.toISOString() }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>
            <span class="post-summary">{{ post.data.summary }}</span>
          </li>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/blog/">All posts on the blog</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
{%- endif %}

    <section class="section download" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="download-title">Download and play</h2>
        <div class="platforms">
          <article class="platform">
            <h3>Windows</h3>
            <p>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and a graphics card that does DirectX&nbsp;11. Nothing to install: everything the game needs is in the zip.</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Download <code>BS3D-…-win-x64.zip</code> from the <a href="{{ site.download }}">newest release</a>.</li>
              <li>Right-click the zip, choose <em>Properties</em> and tick <strong>Unblock</strong> (Windows marks everything it downloads), then extract it.</li>
              <li>Run <code>BS3D.exe</code> from the extracted folder.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="note"><strong>Windows will warn you the first time.</strong> The game is not code-signed (a signing certificate is the one part of this that costs money), so SmartScreen says “Windows protected your PC”. Choose <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</p>
            <p>Your progress and settings live in <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\BS3D</code>, not in the game's folder, so a new version can replace the old folder without losing your save.</p>
            <p><a class="button" href="{{ site.download }}">Download for Windows</a></p>
          </article>
          <article class="platform">
            <h3>Raspberry Pi 5</h3>
            <p>64-bit Raspberry Pi OS. The same game for the Pi's graphics chip: a plainer picture than on Windows ({{ site.piPicture }}).</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Download <code>BS3D-…-linux-arm64.tar.gz</code> from the <a href="{{ site.download }}">newest release</a> and extract it:<code class="cmd">tar xzf BS3D-*-linux-arm64.tar.gz</code></li>
              <li>From a desktop session, run it:<code class="cmd">cd BS3D-*-linux-arm64 &amp;&amp; ./BS3D</code></li>
            </ol>
            <p>Progress and settings live in <code>~/.local/share/BS3D</code>.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="checksums">Every release lists a checksum for each file in <code>SHA256SUMS</code>. The source of everything, the game, its tools and this page, is on <a href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <button class="sound-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false" title="The game's menu music and its cannon's shot, about 1.2 MB, loaded when you press" hidden>
    <svg class="sound-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 9h4l5-4v14l-5-4H4z" fill="currentColor"/><path class="sound-waves" d="M16 8.5a5 5 0 0 1 0 7M18.5 6a8.5 8.5 0 0 1 0 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/><path class="sound-cross" d="M16 9l5 6M21 9l-5 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
    <span class="sound-label">Sound off</span>
  </button>
  <script type="module" src="/js/sound.js"></script>
